WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.400
The Justice

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.601
Department's investigation

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.769
into former President Trump's

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.304
handling of documents

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.839
appears to be far from over.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:06.506
Just this week,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:06.873
the Trump

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:07.374
legal team

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.041
turned over

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.009
even more materials

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.410
with classified markings

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.078
along with a laptop.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.347
They also handed over an empty folder

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.683
marked classified evening briefing.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.385
And joining us now is one of former

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.687
President Trump's attorneys Tim Barletta.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:21.488
All right.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.389
Be to be clear,

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:22.655
the former

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.957
president has a lot of legal issues,

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.226
but you specifically represent him

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.961
in the special counsel's investigation.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.663
Since January six, and Mar a Lago. Yes.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:30.830
All right.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.065
As you just heard, CNN

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.133
and other outlets

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.434
reporting that you handed over

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.102
additional materials, pages

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.504
with classified markings,

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:38.872
a laptop and a thumb

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.740
drive over to investigators.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.143
Tim Trump has been out of office

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.011
for two years.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.746
Why the classified materials

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:47.947
keep showing up.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.350
You know, what has happened here

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.818
that you've seen here

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:52.752
and also in the Biden

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.454
and Pence investigations

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.355
is that

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.322
the White House

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.091
does not have proper procedures

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.626
for handling classified information.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.660
And these documents,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.296
when they get packed up and sent out,

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.798
when people leave office,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:07.567
they do keep showing up, if you will.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.103
We conducted a search back in December,

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.572
which is where we found these documents

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.940
and we turned them over immediately.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.842
These were not turned over last week,

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.511
although the DOJ leaked it last week.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.181
This was turned over back in December.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.349
And so we have gone through

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.018
we've tried to work with the DOJ.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.386
We've tried to do

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.388
searches of all the relevant places.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.457
And anytime we found anything,

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.392
we've immediately turned it over.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.060
And as we understand it, the laptop

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:34.828
that was handed over

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.596
it had scanned copies

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.764
of some of the pages

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.832
that were handed over.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.066
We learned that this laptop

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:40.967
belonged to an aide

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.869
from the Save America pack.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.938
So why would someone from a pack

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.574
have access to classified materials?

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.876
She was working as an aide to

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:50.810
to the president.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.779
And this is a box

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.481
that had all of his daily schedules

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.715
from his time in office.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.551
And she scanned all of those as part of,

00:01:58.885 --> 00:01:59.152
you know,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.153
being available

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.155
for future speeches or

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.057
biographies or things like that.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.391
And after we did

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.526
the search in December,

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.560
and we found that

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.496
within this box of thousands,

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.663
that there were a couple of pages

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.465
that had a little marking at the bottom,

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.134
which we turned over.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:14.701
After that,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.503
we found that she had scanned the box.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.271
So that would be digitized.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.573
She had no idea that there was any

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.710
classification markings on anything.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.512
And as soon as we found out about that,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.579
we called up DOJ

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.614
to let them know

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.349
and immediately provided them

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:30.416
access to it.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.886
Now, you also turned over an empty folder

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.954
marked classified to investigators.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.322
Where was this folder

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.724
and why was it turned over?

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.359
The folder is kind of

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.960
one of the more humorous aspects

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.228
of this whole thing.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.731
This is not a classified folder.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.899
This is a folder

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.967
that when my team went through and search

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.802
and they were up there report,

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.204
which we turned over to DOJ,

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:54.974
they saw it's a it's a folder manila

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.709
folder that says Classified

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.045
evening summary on it.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.181
And it was in the president's bedroom.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.617
He has one of those landline telephones

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.852
next to his bed

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.587
and has a blue light on it,

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.122
and it keeps him up at night.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.290
So he took the manila folder

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.424
and put it over it

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.426
so that it would keep the light down

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.928
so he could sleep at night.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.596
And it's just this folder

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.131
it says classified evening brief

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:18.998
evening summary on

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.467
it is not a classification marking.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.470
It's not anything that is controlled

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.004
in any way.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.406
There's nothing illegal about it.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.141
There's nothing in it.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.176
And when DOJ found out about it,

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.344
they went crazy.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.645
And they said they actually gave me

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:33.513
a subpoena to say,

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:35.582
give us over this empty folder.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.616
That means nothing.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:37.383
How did they find out

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.918
about a folder on his bed table?

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.286
We put it in our report.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.422
We when we did all of our searches,

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.624
we wrote up reports on everywhere.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:45.925
We searched everywhere.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.026
We looked anything.

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:48.995
We found where we found it.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.730
And we gave that to them

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.832
because everything that we've done

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.334
as part of that search has been

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:54.934
in the spirit

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.337
of full cooperation and compliance.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.205
And when they read that and they saw,

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:00.773
oh, there's this folder here

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:01.674
that is

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:02.342
so far

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.776
outside of the scope of the subpoena

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.346
or anything else, they demanded it back.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.248
And so now the president

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.215
has to find a different way

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.750
to keep the blue light out of his lies.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.385
I'm sure he has other options,

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.453
but from wrong.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.854
There's also a similar folder

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:17.390
on display at the Trump Tower Bar.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.225
He is under criminal investigation

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.193
for potentially mishandling

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.361
classified materials.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:21.961
And doesn't

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.496
the use of these folders suggests

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:24.998
somewhat of a flip in attitude

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.733
towards classified materials?

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.533
Not at all.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.001
Not at all.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:28.501
This is

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.369
these are folders

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:30.903
that he was given

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.672
during his time in office.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.607
He didn't keep the contents of the folder

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.776
but the folder itself is interesting.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.378
So he did keep a copy, you know,

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.145
some of the folders.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.881
He put one on display at the 45 bar.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.182
He put one on his phone

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.717
down in Mar a Lago.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.286
When we went through the

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:47.954
the boxes at the National Archives,

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.555
we found a few more of them there.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:49.789
Yeah,

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.858
this is, it's a, it's

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.960
essentially it's a piece of stationery.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.162
It doesn't actually contain anything

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:59.432
controlled or anything.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:00.867
Really? That's a problem.

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:01.801
Oh, he's obviously

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.303
running for president again.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.270
You keep uncovering

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.605
these classified documents

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.606
outside of the settings

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:07.674
in which they belong.

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:08.908
What do you say to people

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.077
who believe that he shouldn't

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:12.679
be trusted with the nation's secrets?

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.480
Nothing that we

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.448
have found

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.884
has any implications on him personally.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.218
Everything that we have found

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.386
has been consistent

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:20.853
with what

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.021
I've been saying from the beginning,

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.022
which is

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:25.892
the White House across administrations.

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:28.261
Their handling of classified documents

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.429
is not the same

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:29.762
as how

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:30.863
the intelligence agencies

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.166
handle it or the military handles it.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:36.202
And so documents are not controlled

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:37.136
in the White House

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:38.871
across administrations.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.107
When people leave the White House

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:43.209
and GSA packs everything up,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:45.378
they get mixed in, as we've seen

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:46.779
with President Trump,

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.781
with President Biden,

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.683
with Vice President Pence.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.685
And really, you know what?

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:55.121
I say here is President Trump.

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:55.555
This doesn't

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:56.522
have anything to do with him.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:57.123
This has to do

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.458
with White House procedures,

00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:00.660
which is one of the reasons why I say

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.562
DOJ should get out of this

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:03.363
and they should instead

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.931
do a review

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:05.898
of what the procedures

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.734
are in the White House

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.503
and then legislative change on how future

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:11.637
White House administrations

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.072
handle documents

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:14.273
that would solve the problem.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:15.007
One big difference

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:15.975
between your client

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.210
and the other two folks

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.177
that you mentioned

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:18.978
is the fact that once

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.179
this issue was raised,

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.180
your client did not

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.382
automatically make an effort

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:23.983
to turn over everything.

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:24.784
It's taken a while.

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:26.252
Things are still being handed over.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:28.388
And it's not just potentially

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:29.822
mishandling classified information.

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:32.158
Your client is also under investigation

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.893
for possible obstruction.

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:35.161
I would disagree with that

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.696
because you're investigating.

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:37.163
Not that,

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:40.233
but that he didn't try to cooperate

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:41.701
from the beginning.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.035
He has tried to cooperate.

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:43.403
In fact,

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:45.538
he had a meeting with the

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.739
with the members of DOJ

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:47.273
where he said,

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:48.241
if there's anything else

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.909
you need, let us know.

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.945
DOJ has taken a position of,

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:53.679
you know, really

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.982
an adversarial position on this,

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.750
where as much as we want to cooperate

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.284
with them,

00:06:58.284 --> 00:06:59.552
they would rather make this

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.920
into an adversarial fight

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.022
and try to make it into a criminal case.

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.290
Had they handled it

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.125
appropriately from the beginning,

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:08.394
agreed to work with us, work

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.228
towards making sure

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:10.763
that we just get the documents

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:12.465
and everything is

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.767
put back into its place.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.202
This all would have been avoided.

00:07:16.202 --> 00:07:17.336
A lot of what you have

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:20.406
here is an appearance of noncompliance,

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:23.543
which is created by DOJ in the manner

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:25.044
in which they have handled this.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:26.145
Are you still searching

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.680
for documents classified?

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.514
We have good markings.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:29.549
Not at this time, no.

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:31.951
We have we have completed our searches

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:34.887
We've given up our reports to DOJ.

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.322
They've seen everything.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.790
This latest

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:38.257
leak from

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:39.792
this past week is really from stuff

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.494
that happened back in December.

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.429
And as the special counsel expressed.

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:43.963
Any interest in

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.331
speaking with your client?

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:47.099
Not to me if he did.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:47.900
Jack Smith is interested

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.302
in asking your client questions.

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:51.103
Would you allow him to do that?

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:52.405
I would certainly consider it,

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:53.506
but I'd like to talk to Jack

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:54.640
Smith himself first.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.775
We haven't talked to Jack Smith yet.

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:57.977
No, but I'd like them. Okay.

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:58.811
Former Vice President

00:07:58.811 --> 00:07:59.812
Mike Pence, as you know,

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:00.713
was recently subpoenaed

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:02.582
in the January 6th investigation.

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:04.650
Do you expect to assert privilege

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.285
to block some of that testimony?

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.154
So as with any witness

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.755
that goes before the grand jury,

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:12.058
we have been instructing them

00:08:12.058 --> 00:08:13.593
to preserve the privilege.

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.294
So any question that they're asked

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:17.230
that doesn't call for privileged answer,

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.232
they should answer any question

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:19.799
that they're asked

00:08:19.799 --> 00:08:21.000
that calls for something

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.635
that is protected by privilege, either

00:08:22.635 --> 00:08:24.937
executive attorney, client or otherwise.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:26.973
They should assert that privilege

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:27.907
at that time.

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:28.107
You know,

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:29.442
they don't give us a list of questions

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:30.576
ahead of time.

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:32.078
They assert the privilege.

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:33.946
And then after they're done testifying,

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:36.315
then it's up to DOJ to decide

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:37.617
whether they want to file

00:08:37.617 --> 00:08:39.752
a motion to compel or not.

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:42.088
And so really,

00:08:42.088 --> 00:08:42.855
all we know

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:44.991
is they want to bring people in.

00:08:44.991 --> 00:08:45.758
And if they're not

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:47.059
going to give us a list of questions

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:48.928
so that we can figure it out. Exactly.

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:49.462
We tell them,

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:51.697
okay, assert privilege to everything.

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:52.965
Because the reality is

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:55.034
you don't want to create a precedent

00:08:55.034 --> 00:08:56.869
where DOJ can just

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.704
run roughshod over the privilege

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:00.573
because it's a new administration.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:02.341
So we instruct them,

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:03.376
they assert,

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:04.644
and then DOJ decides

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:05.411
whether they want to file

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:06.279
a motion to compel.

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:06.979
So it sounds like you

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:09.348
you will likely assert privilege over

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:11.484
the Mike Pence testimony.

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:12.752
Every witness

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:14.186
that goes into the grand jury

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:15.788
that has information

00:09:15.788 --> 00:09:16.923
that's potentially privileged,

00:09:16.923 --> 00:09:18.424
we tell them to assert the privilege.

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:19.292
And that would also apply

00:09:19.292 --> 00:09:19.959
to Robert O'Brien,

00:09:19.959 --> 00:09:21.460
the former national security adviser.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.962
Every witness that goes in

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:23.896
and then as you saw

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:24.931
this week, one additional

00:09:24.931 --> 00:09:26.299
classified document was found

00:09:26.299 --> 00:09:28.000
during a search of vice former Vice

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:28.734
President Mike Pence.

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:29.302
His house

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:30.236
Do you think a special counsel

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:30.870
should be appointed

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.705
to look into his case?

00:09:32.705 --> 00:09:33.673
I don't

00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:34.974
I don't think that there should be

00:09:34.974 --> 00:09:36.075
special counsel's

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:38.044
appointed to look at any classified

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:39.211
document cases

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.413
I think that that is a business

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:41.581
that DOJ needs to be

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.115
put on the bench for.

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:44.850
And instead, the office of the Director

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.118
of National Intelligence

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:47.286
should get into it,

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:47.820
and they should do

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.555
an administrative classify

00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:51.891
document spillage investigation

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:53.192
they should provide

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:55.261
to all former residents

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:56.295
of the White House.

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:58.230
They should provide them all amnesty.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.865
That way they can get full cooperate

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:01.834
from everybody and figure out really

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.469
what is going on

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:04.904
with the White House document

00:10:04.904 --> 00:10:06.205
handling procedures

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:07.740
so that they can fix it.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.909
When you have DOJ go into these things,

00:10:09.909 --> 00:10:11.978
they are automatically going in

00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:13.779
with all the criminal processes

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:14.714
and trying to threaten

00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:16.983
people to go to jail over

00:10:16.983 --> 00:10:18.150
something that really is

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.252
a procedural failure

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:22.321
and an institutional procedural failure

00:10:22.655 --> 00:10:25.591
that has nothing to do with Mike Pence,

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:28.961
Donald Trump or quite frankly, Joe Biden.

00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:30.229
All right.

00:10:30.229 --> 00:10:31.063
We have to leave it there.

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:32.131
Thanks so much for joining us.

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:34.133
Appreciate. Clearly a lot to talk about.

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:34.900
Thank you for having me.

